ind('facebook-page-restricted-for-car-dealerships','Car dealerships','Facebook Page','Car Dealership Facebook Page or Ads Restricted: What to Do (2026)','<strong>For a car dealership, start in Business Support Home to see whether the Page, the ad account or the admin profile is restricted.</strong> Vehicle ads with financing terms fall under Meta’s financial products rules. Fix the flagged ad, then request one review. Meta makes the final decision.',['Financing or credit offers in ads, which fall under Special Ad Categories.','Marketplace listings that break Commerce Policies.','Several staff logging in to one personal profile.','Sudden spend increases on a new ad account.'],[('Can my sales staff share one login?','No. Give each person their own admin role in the Business Portfolio.'),('Our Marketplace access is gone. Is that the Page?','No. Marketplace access is tied to a personal profile.')]),
ind('instagram-disabled-for-med-spas-and-clinics','Med spas and clinics','Instagram','Med Spa Instagram or Ads Disabled: What to Do (2026)','<strong>For a med spa, first check whether the Instagram account itself is disabled or only the ads are restricted.</strong> Before-and-after photos and health claims are common triggers. Appeal from the notice or Business Support Home once, in plain words. Meta makes the final decision.',['Before-and-after images in ads.','Claims about results of treatments.','Targeting or wording that implies a personal health condition.','Booking links that redirect several times.'],[('Can we post before-and-after photos?','Organic posts follow Community Guidelines. Ads have stricter rules; check Meta’s advertising standards.'),('Our account and ads went down together. Which first?','The account. Ad access depends on the profile behind it.')]),
ind('facebook-page-restricted-for-hotels-and-guesthouses','Hotels and guesthouses','Facebook Page','Hotel Facebook Page or Instagram Restricted: What to Do (2026)','<strong>For a hotel, check whether the restriction is on the Page, an admin profile or the ad account.</strong> Copycat pages and hacked admin profiles are common. Recover the admin first, remove unknown admins, then request one review. Meta makes the final decision.',['A hacked admin profile used to post scam offers.','Impersonating pages reporting your real Page.','Promotions that look like giveaways without rules.','Shared logins among front-desk staff.'],[('A fake page copies our hotel. What can we do?','Report it as impersonation from your Page. Keep screenshots.'),('Front desk shares one login. Is that a problem?','Yes. Give each person their own role.')]),
mk('client-fired-agency-removed-access','Client Fired the Agency and Removed Access: Facebook, Instagram, Ads','Client removed agency access','When a client ends work with your agency and removes your access to their Page, ad account or Business Portfolio: what is normal, what to hand back, and what to keep.','The client fired us and removed our access.','It happens. Here is what is normal, and what to keep for your records.','<strong>When a client removes your agency from their Business Portfolio, you lose access to their assets, and that is how Meta permissions work.</strong> Hand back anything you own on their behalf, keep invoices and reports, and do not try to log in through old personal credentials. Disputes over ownership are a legal matter, not a Meta appeal.',[('Normal','Owners can remove partners.'),('Hand back','Pages or ad accounts you created for them.'),('Keep','Invoices and reports.')],'<h2 id="what-to-do">What to do</h2><ol><li>Check which assets in your own Business Portfolio belong to the client and transfer them.</li><li>Remove your payment method from any ad account you funded.</li><li>Keep exports of reports you are entitled to.</li><li>Do not use old staff logins to get back in. It can get your own profile restricted.</li></ol>',[('ads','Business tools',[AQ,BV,ADS[0]])],[SEND],L('former-employee-still-admin','former employee still admin')+', '+L('for-agencies-banned-client-accounts','agency hub')+'.',[('Can the client take a Page we created?','If the Page was created for them, transferring it is normal practice. Ownership disputes are a legal matter.'),('Our ad account was paying for their ads. What now?','Remove your payment method and settle the balance with Meta.')]),
mk('former-employee-still-admin','Former Employee Still Admin on Your Facebook Page or Business Portfolio','Former employee still admin','A former employee or freelancer still has admin access to your Facebook Page, Instagram or Business Portfolio. How to remove them, and what to do if they removed you.','A former employee is still an admin.','Remove access before it becomes a problem.','<strong>If a former employee is still an admin, remove them in Business Portfolio settings under People, or in Page access settings.</strong> If they hold the only full control and will not hand it back, collect proof the business owns the asset and use Meta’s business help routes. Meta makes the final decision.',[('Remove','People settings.'),('Locked out','Prove ownership.'),('Prevent','Two admins minimum.')],'<h2 id="steps">Steps</h2><ol><li>Open Business Portfolio settings, then People, and remove the person.</li><li>Check Page access and Instagram account access separately.</li><li>Rotate shared passwords and remove unknown devices.</li><li>Keep at least two admins you trust.</li></ol><p>If they removed you, gather business registration, domain email and invoices that show the business owns the asset.</p>',[('ads','Business tools',[AQ,BV,ADS[0]])],[SEND],L('client-fired-agency-removed-access','client removed agency access')+', '+L('for-agencies-banned-client-accounts','agency hub')+'.',[('The ex-employee removed me as admin. Can I get it back?','Sometimes, through Meta’s business help with proof of ownership. It is not automatic.'),('Should we share one login?','No. Shared logins are a common reason for security checks and restrictions.')]),
